{% comment %}
  snippets/labor-day-sale-note.liquid

  Price-adjacent sale note on eligible PDPs, keyed to ACTUAL discount eligibility
  (collection membership), not the product title. Replaces the previous
  title-string block in the four product templates (main-product, -comb,
  -variants, -home-gym-packages).

  Accepts:
    product         (Product)  required
    section_id      (string)   required for variant-aware updates. Pass section.id - it
                               is not in scope inside a {% render %}. It builds the
                               container id that assets/product-info.js swaps on variant
                               change; without it the card keeps the first variant's
                               prices. The two copies get distinct ids so both update.
    hide_on_mobile  (boolean)  optional. Pass true on the desktop-layout copy so it
                               does not also render on mobile (the mobile-layout copy
                               is rendered without it and is the one shown on phones).

  ELIGIBILITY: mirrors each discount collection's own smart-collection rules, read from
  non-truncating product fields (vendor / type / tags / title). It deliberately does NOT
  use product.collections, which truncates when a product is in more than ~20 collections
  (so the eligible collection could be missed), and it does NOT depend on the collection
  being published to the Online Store. The automatic discounts still target the
  collections by ID, so this note matches exactly which products get discounted.
    French Fitness 10% (collection 519462814012, all must be true):
      vendor == 'French Fitness' AND type != 'Product (Hidden)' AND no 'july4-exclude' or 'labor-day-price-marked' tag
    Remanufactured 5% (collection 512180715836, all must be true):
      title contains 'Remanufactured' AND type == 'Product Index'

  DISPLAY: renders as a compact sale card, not a free-text paragraph. The card sits
  directly beneath the main price block so its struck-through "was" figure reads as the
  page price being crossed out. Both figures are computed in Liquid from the same variant
  price the main price block renders (selected_or_first_available_variant), rather than
  read from settings.sale_promo_ff / settings.sale_promo_reman, so they always match the
  real discount. Those two settings still gate the card per branch (blank = hidden).

  The strikethrough is presentational only: a plain <span> with a CSS line-through inside
  the card. The main price element and the product structured data are deliberately left
  alone - the price Google crawls stays the official price, matching the product feed.

  Because both figures are variant-specific, the card must re-render when the shopper
  picks a different variant. product-info.js only swaps elements it names by id, so the
  container carries LaborDaySaleCard-<section id> (mobile copy) or
  LaborDaySaleCard-Desktop-<section id> (the hide_on_mobile copy) and both ids are in
  that script's update list. Rename one and the card silently goes stale.

  END DATE: settings.laborday_end is an EXCLUSIVE boundary (the window check below stops
  rendering at that instant), so formatting it verbatim would advertise one day too many.
  The fine print shows the last day the sale is actually live: end - 1 second.
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign in_ff = false
  assign in_reman = false

  if product.vendor == 'French Fitness' and product.type != 'Product (Hidden)'
    unless product.tags contains 'july4-exclude' or product.tags contains 'labor-day-price-marked'
      assign in_ff = true
    endunless
  endif

  if product.type == 'Product Index' and product.title contains 'Remanufactured'
    assign in_reman = true
  endif

  comment
    September Overstock Sale. Unlike the two campaigns above, that automatic discount
    targets an EXPLICIT LIST OF 16 PRODUCT IDS, not a collection, so there is no
    vendor/type/tag rule to mirror - membership is the id list in
    settings.overstock_product_ids. Delimit both sides with commas before matching so
    one id cannot match inside a longer one.
  endcomment
  assign in_overstock = false
  assign os_ids = settings.overstock_product_ids | newline_to_br | replace: '<br />', ',' | replace: '<br/>', ',' | replace: '<br>', ',' | replace: ' ', '' | replace: ',,', ','
  if os_ids != blank
    assign os_haystack = ',' | append: os_ids | append: ','
    assign os_needle = ',' | append: product.id | append: ','
    if os_haystack contains os_needle
      assign in_overstock = true
    endif
  endif

  comment
    campaign_kind drives which payoff line renders below. The settings.sale_promo_ff /
    settings.sale_promo_reman text fields are no longer displayed verbatim - the payoff
    line is computed from product.price - but a blank field still acts as a per-branch
    kill switch, same as before, so merchants can turn a branch off without a code edit.
  endcomment
  assign campaign_kind = ''
  if in_ff and settings.sale_promo_ff != blank
    assign campaign_kind = 'ff'
  elsif in_reman and settings.sale_promo_reman != blank
    assign campaign_kind = 'reman'
  endif
-%}
{%- comment -%}
  Overstock window (store timezone), evaluated separately from the Labor Day window
  because the two campaigns run on different dates.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign os_now_s = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
{%- assign os_start_s = settings.overstock_start | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
{%- assign os_end_s = settings.overstock_end | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
{%- assign os_in_window = false -%}
{%- if settings.overstock_force_preview or request.design_mode -%}
  {%- assign os_in_window = true -%}
{%- elsif os_start_s > 0 and os_end_s > 0 and os_now_s >= os_start_s and os_now_s < os_end_s -%}
  {%- assign os_in_window = true -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%} Date window (store timezone). Theme editor and force_preview both bypass it. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign now_s = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
{%- assign start_s = settings.laborday_start | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
{%- assign end_s = settings.laborday_end | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
{%- assign in_window = false -%}
{%- if settings.laborday_force_preview or request.design_mode -%}
  {%- assign in_window = true -%}
{%- elsif start_s > 0 and end_s > 0 and now_s >= start_s and now_s < end_s -%}
  {%- assign in_window = true -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- liquid
  comment
    Only one automatic discount applies at checkout, so only one card may render.
    Precedence must be decided AFTER in_window exists: campaign_kind is set from
    eligibility alone, so a French Fitness product still reads as 'ff' once Labor Day
    has ended. Overstock therefore takes over whenever the Labor Day / Remanufactured
    card is not actually going to render - either no branch matched, or its window has
    closed. During the overlap both are 10% off for French Fitness, so the figure is
    identical either way and the shopper never sees the precedence change.
  endcomment
  assign labor_card_showing = false
  if campaign_kind != '' and in_window
    assign labor_card_showing = true
  endif

  assign os_eligible = false
  if in_overstock and settings.overstock_enabled and os_in_window
    assign os_eligible = true
  endif

  comment
    overstock_force_preview must outrank a live Labor Day card, or the switch cannot do
    what its label promises. Most Overstock products are also Labor Day eligible, so
    while both campaigns overlap the Labor Day branch wins and QA has no way to see the
    Overstock card at all - it would only appear once Labor Day expired, which is far
    too late to test it. The explicit QA switch therefore takes precedence; normal
    date-driven precedence is unchanged when it is off.
  endcomment
  if os_eligible
    if settings.overstock_force_preview
      assign campaign_kind = 'overstock'
    elsif labor_card_showing == false
      assign campaign_kind = 'overstock'
    endif
  endif
-%}
{%- liquid
  comment
    Suppress the offer when the selected variant cannot be purchased. Mirror the
    native buy-buttons availability and minimum-quantity gate; do not alter stock.
    Preview mode bypasses dates only, never availability or discount eligibility.
  endcomment
  assign campaign_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign campaign_available = false
  if campaign_variant != blank and campaign_variant.available
    assign campaign_available = true
    if campaign_variant.inventory_management == 'shopify' and campaign_variant.inventory_policy != 'continue'
      if campaign_variant.quantity_rule.min > campaign_variant.inventory_quantity
        assign campaign_available = false
      endif
    endif
  endif
  assign show_campaign = false
  if campaign_kind == 'overstock'
    comment
      Overstock already passed its own window check above; in_window belongs to Labor Day.
    endcomment
    if campaign_available
      assign show_campaign = true
    endif
  elsif campaign_kind != '' and in_window and campaign_available
    assign show_campaign = true
  endif
-%}
{%- if show_campaign -%}
  {%- liquid
    comment
      Mirror the main price block, which renders with use_variant: true - product.price is
      the family MINIMUM and would strike through a figure the shopper never sees.
    endcomment
    assign card_price = campaign_variant.price
    assign card_badge = 'Labor day sale'
    if campaign_kind == 'reman'
      assign card_discount = '5% off'
      assign card_sale_price = card_price | times: 0.95
    elsif campaign_kind == 'overstock'
      assign card_badge = 'September overstock sale'
      assign card_discount = '10% off'
      assign card_sale_price = card_price | times: 0.9
    else
      assign card_discount = '10% off'
      assign card_sale_price = card_price | times: 0.9
    endif
    comment
      laborday_end is exclusive - back off one second so the copy names the last day the
      sale is actually live (an end of Sep 8 00:00 reads as "Ends Sep. 7").
    endcomment
    assign card_end_s = end_s
    if campaign_kind == 'overstock'
      assign card_end_s = os_end_s
    endif
    assign last_day_s = card_end_s | minus: 1
  -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Keep both update targets even when empty. product-info.js replaces innerHTML only
  when both old and new IDs exist, so removing the wrapper makes sold-out/available
  variant transitions stale. Whitespace trimming plus :empty removes the empty gap.
{%- endcomment -%}
  <div
    {% if section_id != blank %}id="LaborDaySaleCard{% if hide_on_mobile %}-Desktop{% endif %}-{{ section_id }}"{% endif %}
    class="campaign-sale-container{% if hide_on_mobile %} hide-on-mobile{% endif %}"
  >
    {%- if show_campaign -%}
    <div class="labor-day-sale-card">
      <div class="labor-day-sale-card__row">
        <span class="labor-day-sale-card__badge">{{ card_badge }}</span>
        <span class="labor-day-sale-card__was"
          ><span class="visually-hidden">Regular price </span>{{ card_price | money }}</span
        >
        <span class="labor-day-sale-card__now"
          ><span class="visually-hidden">Sale price </span>{{ card_sale_price | money }} in cart</span
        >
      </div>
      <p class="labor-day-sale-card__meta">
        {{ card_discount }} applied automatically at checkout{% if card_end_s > 0 %} · Ends {{ last_day_s | date: "%b. %-d" }}{% endif %}
      </p>
    </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .campaign-sale-container:empty {
    display: none !important;
    margin: 0 !important;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
